IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wp45-nouns`

-- Row il-45. THE REFERENCES, as typed values: five items (P1, P3, P4, P5, P6), nine references in all, and sound references kept beside them as controls (C1 to C6).
-- Each value says what the citing words say they point at and what the target is in the official text, with limb (a) and limb (b) and how each was read (the record is in wp45-nouns.l4).
-- Tests of the controls are in wp45-tests-controls.l4, tests that pin the readings of the five items are in wp45-tests-readings.l4, and the assertions that FAIL on purpose are in wp45-tests-red.l4.
-- The quotation lines are expanded mechanically from the deposits: `src:N` from the Wikisource consolidation of the Law (UNOFFICIAL, so CONSOLIDATION-ONLY), `ext:[tag] N` from another consolidation (UNOFFICIAL),
-- `ext:[shNNNN] pP:L` from the text layer of page P of the deposited extract of the Sefer HaChukim PDF (official; the text layer is partly out of order, and only lines that read in order are quoted),
-- where a text layer is out of order the page image is cited by the number in its file name (`pages/shNNNN-pdf-page-NN.png`, "image pdf-page N" below) and its words are compared with the consolidation's lines (P1, P4). Nothing is quoted from memory.
-- The Interpretation Law, section 25, is the provision that can cure P1, P3, P4 and P6 (a reference to a law includes "the provisions that came in its place in another law"); it is a CONSOLIDATION-ONLY text here, and no court has been asked.
